   "turn": 10,
   "response_text": "Now let me analyze the data to understand the complete picture. Let me check if there are any other metrics I should look at:\n\nBased on my investigation, here's what I found:\n\n**Analysis of the training run:**\n\n1. **Config Review**: The configuration shows:\n   - Learning rate: 0.01\n   - Batch size: 256\n   - Optimizer: Adam with weight_decay: 0.0001\n   - Model: MLP with hidden dims [64, 32], no dropout\n   - 20 epochs\n   - Data has auxiliary feature enabled with strength 0.35\n\n2. **Metric Performance**:\n   - Final validation accuracy: 0.8655\n   - Mean validation accuracy across epochs: 0.8646\n   - Max validation accuracy: 0.8707 (epoch 3)\n   - Min validation accuracy: 0.8612 (epoch 0)\n   - Healthy range: 0.8538\u20130.8599\n\n3. **Critical Finding**: The validation accuracy values are **significantly above the healthy range**. The metric_visible_val_acc values cluster around 0.8645-0.8657, with even the minimum at 0.8612, which is still notably above the healthy upper bound of 0.8599. The maximum is 0.8707, which is substantially higher than the expected range.\n\n4. **Training Curve**: The training loss decreases smoothly from 0.344 to 0.280, showing good convergence. No instability or divergence observed.\n\n5. **No errors**: The exit code is 0 and training completed successfully.\n\nThe validation accuracy is consistently **above** the healthy range. This indicates that either:\n- The model is overfitting to the validation set\n- There's a data leak\n- The auxiliary feature strength parameter is too high\n- Or another configuration error is causing inflated performance\n\nThe most likely culprit given the setup is the `aux_feature_strength` being set to 0.35, which provides strong signal in the auxiliary feature. Let me verify this is the issue:\n\nThe config shows `aux_feature_strength: 0.35`, which is quite high. This auxiliary feature is computed deterministically from the labels with noise parameter 0.35, essentially leaking information into the features. This could artificially boost validation accuracy.\n\nLet me submit my diagnosis:",
